OL,3,CDrinking bans during football matches
OL,4,Cshould be scrapped, Burnham says
OL,6,FBans on football fans drinking in the
OL,7,Fstands during matches are outdated,
OL,8,Fdiscriminatory and should be scrapped,
OL,9,Fthe prime minister has said.
OL,11,FAndy Burnham, who is an Everton fan,
OL,12,Fsaid it was unfair for football fans
OL,13,Fto be singled out when the supporters
OL,14,Fof other sports are able to drink
OL,15,Fwhile watching their teams.
OL,17,FThe ban was put in place during the
OL,18,F1980s when concerns about hooliganism
OL,19,Fwere at their height and covers the
OL,20,Ftop five tiers of English men's
OL,21,Ffootball.
OL,1,W~s1{$~k4{$k7                    G1/10
OL,2,W,.!/  +.!/*%*%R,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
